\end{align*}
Here, the nonlinear term $f_i$ depends on $g$, which is restricted to a manifold $M$ embedded within a Banach space $X$. Specifically, $f_i = F_i(g)$ for some single-valued branches $F_i$, with $f_i = G_i(f)$ replaced by conditions on $F_i$. Our primary objective involves characterizing all possible solutions $(f_1, \dots, f_n)$ through the relation $f_i=F_i(g)$ for $i=1,\dots,n$. Under conditions imposed on the function $F_i$, we demonstrate the presence of multiple solution structures, identified as manifolds with positive codimension. Additionally, under more restrictive assumptions on $F_i$, it is further shown that additional solutions exist which are not captured by the previously characterized families.

